From 0528db5e08b3286f565149a3186b03ba48c7c038 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:36:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/31] fix(token-capture): hash empty assistant turns so their
 calls stay resolvable

assistant_fingerprint hashed only the content parts and tool calls of
model-authored items, and _content_of drops empty text. A reply with no
text and no tool call therefore added nothing to the hash, so the call
that produced it got the same continuation fingerprint as its parent.
The next request matched both ledger rows, both recorded contexts were a
prefix of it, and the resolver refused to choose: FileLineageStore
._resolve_row returns None for more than one row (reported as no_match),
RolloutLineage.resolve_node reports ambiguous. The call was poisoned as
unresolved_parent and every later call of the rollout followed.

Evidence (job 5256202, Terminus-2 on a pretraining checkpoint, 1404/2380
replies empty): 62/192 rollouts rejected with unresolved_parent. In all
62 the ledger holds two committed rows with the same fingerprint right
before the first unresolved call; none of the 130 accepted rollouts has
a repeated fingerprint.

Fix: a turn is a run of consecutive model-authored items (standalone
reasoning items are skipped and do not split a run). A run that hashed no
field gets an explicit marker. Non-empty turns hash exactly as before, so
the golden vectors are unchanged; content ""/None/[]/empty text blocks
still hash identically, and tool-call-only turns (content None or "", or
an empty Responses message next to a function_call) hash as before.
FINGERPRINT_VERSION goes to 2 because fingerprints of histories with an
empty turn change; rows stamped by an older model server are then
ignored (fail closed) instead of compared across canonicalizations.

Tests: new fingerprint and ledger cases, plus the reproduction suite
test_token_capture_empty_assistant.py (10 former strict xfails now pass,
13 controls unchanged).

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
